Z||000000||voyagerspe||03-17-2001||12:16 AM||||hi I just put the first 100 miles on my 87 gt<BR>after putting in a new motor.  I bought the car with a bad motor and only drove it home.  The engine has lots of power but the trans. seems to be very "slushy" the shifts are weak .  There is only 67000 on the car and tranny so i dont think that the tranny is failing but im not sure.  I serviced the tranny the oil was clean and bright with no burnt smell.  Is this just the way these trannys are?  Should I put in a shift kit? will it make a difference?  Has anyone else had the same problem?  Am I just spoiled by turbo 400 trannys in my previous toys? thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||MontanaFiero||03-17-2001||02:52 AM||||Mine feels solid (my tranny, of course). Unless you are talking about that annoying "slip" they do when shifting from 2 to 3. I have heard that's common, and correctable with a shift kit.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||03-17-2001||10:07 AM||||I never thought the shifts on my tranny felt slushy.  I have been afraid that they were a little too harsh when it shifts.  Especially from 1-2 under hard acceleration, I get a good kick while shifting.  Under normal accel it shifts very smooth.  Maybe your trans shifts.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||03-17-2001||11:50 AM||||If the T.V. (throttle valve) cable is adjusted incorrectly, or not connected at all, it will cause your trans to shift very early and very mushy.  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000004||voyagerspe||03-17-2001||12:46 PM||||ill try adjusting the t.v. cable.  then if that doesnt help Ill put in a shift kit.  <BR>1st to 2nd isnt that bad but 2nd to 3rd is awful. Thanks for your help ill let you know if it works||||reg||1
